  "relevance_note": "One in-scope person: cohort patient 26, whose Table 3 row reads 'TNFAIP3 {c.1217A>T, p.E406V}', is the only person in the paper with a TNFAIP3 variant, and that row gives individual-level sex, ages and clinical features.",
  "method_note": "Read the paper directly; no script transcribed tables, Table 3 row 26 was transcribed by hand and re-checked against the Markdown. Scope: only patient 26 of the 32 uAID patients carries a TNFAIP3 variant, so the other cohort members (variants in other genes, or no variant) get no rows and are counted in cohort_size_as_stated = 32; patients mentioned only as literature groups (e.g. the 22-patient uAID series, the 81-year-old and 42-year-old from ref 9) have no TNFAIP3 variant or HA20 diagnosis and are out of scope. n_patients_reported = 1 is my count of patients with a TNFAIP3 variant in this paper, not a number the authors state. Table 3 prints no legend for its **+**/**-** symbols (the table notes only list abbreviations): I recorded **+** cells as observed and, following the v3 table-symbol rule, left the **-** cells as not reported because no legend or text defines them as absent or negative; Table 3 does distinguish '-' from its empty cells. Contradiction/oddity: Table 2 lists TNFAIP3 c.1217A>T, p.E406V, but the ACMG paragraph classifies only C8B, TREX1, NFAT5, PSMB8, STAT2, TNFRSF1B, IL23R, IL10, PTHR1 and STAT4 variants, so pathogenicity and ACMG criteria are not reported for this variant. Ages in Table 3 carry no units in the table itself; Table 1 states 'Onset age, years' and 'Age of the diagnosis, years', so 5.7 and 14.7 were read as years and converted as P5Y7M / P14Y7M. The 'Laboratory activity' **+** cell was taken as the elevated-inflammatory-marker item on the checklist. The paper also states 'All patients also had a formal diagnosis of sJIA to qualify for biologic treatment.'; that group statement was not used as a disease label. is_proband and cites_prior_report_of_same_patients are false; the spans given for them are the nearest supporting text, since no quote can assert a negative.",
